511 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 219 0 R /Rect [ 113.198997 550.646945 481.768005 745.232943 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure2) /TU (Diagram of Astrocyte Gating Mechanism showing a flowchart with components: Local Activity Inputs including Membrane Potential, Synaptic Input, and Output Spike. These feed into Local Drive, Slow State Integrator \(Leaky Filter\), Layer-wise Normalization, and Sigmoid Gating Function, resulting in Gating Factor. A graph depicting the Sigmoid Function is included.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
512 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 219 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 228.032992 538.587036 473.486972 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure3) /TU (Flowchart illustrating the online processing loop from time one to time T for neuron processing. It includes stages like previous and current layer spikes, synapse-local eligibility trace, astrocyte-like regulation, homeostatic stabilization, error broadcast, and loss calculation. Components interact through arrows indicating data flow, such as synaptic weights, membrane potential, and modulatory signals. The process culminates in output error comparison against target labels for weight updates.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
